# What is a workbook

"The atom of a living internet." The three claims — it's the glue, it becomes anything, it carries its own infrastructure — over the DNA-strip canvas.

client :workbook do
  <section id="s2">
  <div id="dna"><canvas id="dnaCv" aria-hidden="true"></canvas></div>
    <div class="sky-pin">
      <canvas id="tree" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
      <div class="sky-content">
        <div class="sky-head">
          <p class="sky-kicker">what is a workbook <b>■</b> 01</p>
          <h2 class="sky-h">the atom of <em>a living internet.</em></h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sky-foot">
          <ul class="sky-points">
            <li><b>It's the glue.</b> One agnostic format for any data, any system, any language — people, services, and code all meet in the same file.</li>
            <li><b>It becomes anything.</b> The same workbook ships as a mobile app, a desktop app, or a website — no porting, no rebuilds.</li>
            <li><b>It carries its own infrastructure.</b> Every workbook runs a sandbox for its code, a database for its state, and agents that keep it building.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
